# Ratchet for warning-level findings from `verikt check` on this repository.
#
# These are real findings, not false positives: functions over the 50-line limit in
# code-quality.md, plus advisory anti-patterns. Generated code is excluded via
# check.exclude in verikt.yaml, so everything counted here is hand-written. They do not fail the
# build, because only error severity does — but without a ceiling they accumulate
# unnoticed, and "warnings we live with" quietly becomes the baseline.
#
# The self-check CI job fails if the count rises above this number. Lower it when
# you pay debt down; raising it should be a deliberate, reviewed decision with a
# reason in the commit message.
78
